Subject: [RESEARCH, NOT APPLIED] extend the dated fee table's verified-through date to 16 Nov 2026

The frozen table at `nse_equity_index_options_rates_20261009_v1` is PRESERVED by this patch
being a patch: nothing in `research/replay/fee_models.py` is changed on the review branch, and
earlier research keeps the exact table it ran against. Apply this only after reviewing the
evidence below.

WHAT IT CHANGES  Two lines. `RATES_VERIFIED_THROUGH` moves from 2026-10-09 to 2026-11-16, which
extends the LAST window (`nse_idx_opt_20260401`, whose `end` is that constant) and nothing else;
`RATES_TABLE_VERSION` is bumped because the version names the audited state of the table.
No rate moves. No window is added, because no component changed its value after 1 April 2026 --
had one changed, the correct edit would be a NEW window starting on its effective date, never a
widened one.

WHY IT IS JUSTIFIED  All six components were checked against a primary or issuing source, with
the retrievals dated 16 November 2026 (IST). Per component:

  1. STT, sale of an option -- 0.15% of premium, payable by the seller, w.e.f. 1 April 2026.
     NSE, "SEBI Turnover Fees, STT and Other levies" (page states "Updated on: 17/04/2026"),
     https://www.nseindia.com/static/invest/first-time-investor-sebi-turnover-fees-stt-other-levies
     Corroborated by Upstox's dated schedule: "STT/CTT (From 1st April 2026) ... Equity Options
     0.15% on sell side (on premium)".

  2. SEBI turnover fee -- Rs.10 per crore (0.0001%) on all sale and purchase transactions.
     Same NSE page. Corroborated: Upstox "SEBI Charges ... Rs.10/crore".

  3. Stamp duty, equity options -- 0.003%, buyer. Same NSE page. Corroborated: Upstox
     "Stamp Duty ... Equity Options 0.003% or Rs.300 / crore on buy side".

  4. GST -- 18% on brokerage and the exchange charges. Same NSE page. Corroborated: Upstox
     "GST ... 18% (on brokerage + transaction charges + IPFT charges)".

  5. Exchange transaction charge -- Rs.3,552.99 per crore of traded PREMIUM value, each side.
  6. NSE IPFT contribution   -- Rs.0.01 per crore of traded premium value, each side.
     PRIMARY SOURCE, read in full: NSE/FA/73061, "Revision in Transaction Charges",
     27 February 2026, https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/content/circulars/FA73061.pdf
     Its table reads, for "Equity Options (on premium)", revised outflow: transaction charges
     "Rs. 3,552.99 each side", contribution to NSE IPFT "Rs. 0.01 each side", total "Rs. 3,553
     each side", and: "The above revision will be applicable with effect from March 1, 2026."
     Both table values therefore match the issuing circular exactly, including the split.

  7. Brokerage -- Rs.20 per executed order. Upstox, https://upstox.com/brokerage-charges/
     retrieved 16 November 2026: "Equity Options -- Flat Rs.20 per executed order". This is a
     commercial tariff, not a statutory rate, so it is the one component with no regulator
     behind it and the one most likely to move without notice.

WHAT IS STILL NOT PROVEN, AND MUST BE WEIGHED BEFORE APPLYING

  * I could not establish from NSE's OWN circular listing that no FA-series circular after
    9 October 2026 revised components 5 or 6. The JSON endpoint I tried
    (`/api/circulars?dept=FA&from_date=..&to_date=..`) returned `{"data":[]}` for the October-
    November window AND for a February-March window that is KNOWN to contain FA/73061, so the
    endpoint or its parameters are wrong and the empty result carries no information. I am not
    treating it as evidence of absence.
    What stands in its place is weaker but real: three independent broker schedules retrieved
    today (Upstox, Zerodha, mstock) all present "from 1 March 2026 / 0.03553% on premium" as the
    CURRENT window, with no later one listed. Brokers bill these charges and update these pages
    when a circular lands, so their dated windows are a reasonable, though secondary, check.
    If you want the absence proven at the source, the remaining step is the circulars list at
    nseindia.com/resources/exchange-communication-circulars for the Finance & Accounts series
    after 9 October 2026.

  * Upstox's page is internally inconsistent about IPFT: its dated table says "Rs.0.01 per crore
    ... (On Premium)" (agreeing with the circular) while a prose block further down still says
    "Rs.0.50/lakh on Equity Options premium" -- the PRE-rollback figure that FA/73061 explicitly
    reversed. The circular governs, and the table holds the circular's value. Recorded here
    because a reader checking that page alone would find the contradiction.

WHAT APPLYING IT UNBLOCKS, MEASURED  With the window extended and nothing else changed, on the
12 November capture: 240 of 318 NIFTY BUY rows and 244 of 323 BANKNIFTY BUY rows carry
`fee_rates_unknown_for_trade_date` AND NOTHING ELSE, so they become scorable. The rest are
refused for reasons that are not fee-related (72/73 rows have no 60-minute hold window inside a
capture that stops at 13:40/13:45; 6 rows per index are each contract's final poll, with no
fill).

UNTIL IT IS APPLIED  After-cost coverage stays at exactly zero, by construction, and Stage D
reports the fee window as the single blocker rather than estimating a cost it cannot source.

